  "details": "<p>Size and location of Camp I are supporting evidence for candidacy of\u00a0<a class=\"internal-link\" href=\"../92147/pitcairlie-hill-carpow\" title=\"Pitcairlie Hill (Carpow)\">Pitcairlie Hill (Carpow)</a> as site of <a class=\"internal-link\" href=\"../92147\" title=\"Graupius M.\">Graupius M.</a></p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Multi-period site consisting of two Roman temporary camps and a later legionary fortress. The first camp is thought to be from the Flavian period, while the fortress is of Severan date. Cited: BAtlas 9 D4 Carpow",
